cable to a computer). Most connector types are available in one of two genders--male or female. A male connector is characterized by one or more exposed pins; a female connector is characterized by one or more receptacles--sockets or jacks-- designed to accept the pins on the male connector.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="38186">connector</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2913040">conector</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12065_235429_1538551"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A report that summarizes the status of an account, including current balance and recent activities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235429">statement</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1538551">instrución</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12068_27187_497396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A marketing program designed to accomplish a specific result, such as introducing a new product or increasing market share.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27187">campaign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497396">campaña<