 id="412277">sistema de transferencia de mensaxes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1421_145137_2785686"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A network type that a computer is connected to that automatically sets the appropriate firewall settings for the location.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145137">network location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2785686">localización de rede</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14210_2307008_2772070"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The act of reducing the probability and/or impact of a risk to an acceptable level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2307008">mitigation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2772070">mitigación</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14210_252102_2772070"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The act of reducing the probability and/or impact of a risk to an acceptable level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="252102">risk mitigation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2772070">mitigación</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14211_213519_2638685"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An order for a SKU that is currently not available for delivery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="213519">pre-order</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2638685">pedido anticipado</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14212_338602_2016110"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The status message displayed for the current network when a user changes the network selection to something other than the network of the main provider.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="338602">Home service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2016110">servizo local</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14216_397178_412257"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of recipients that are created to expedite the mass emailing of messages and other information. When email is sent to a mail-enabled universal distribution group, all members of that list receive a copy of the message. Mail-enabled universal distribution groups cannot be used to assign permissions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397178">mail-enabled universal distribution group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="412257">rolda de distribución universal habilitada para correo electrónico</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14219_310257_498836"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows technology that protects OS resources (files, folders registry keys) and prevents applications and administrators from making changes to a computer's resources in an arbitrary way.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="310257">System Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498836">Protección do sistema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14232_231970_498444"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that provides interactive analysis of data, like a PivotTable report. You can change views of data, see different levels of detail, or reorganize the chart layout by dragging fields and by showing or hiding items in fields.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231970">PivotChart report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498444">informe de gráfica dinámica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14237_169312_2767500"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database that functions as a backup of a primary database, receiving copies of every change to the primary database, and that can take over traffic if the primary database becomes unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="169312">mirror database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2767500">base de datos reflectida</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14238_2822_497227"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A memory measurement unit that is equal to 1 million bytes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2822">MB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497227">MB</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalG