ervice provider (OSP).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="776387">online identity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178910">identidade en liña</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20960_760162_1178911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A provider of online services like email, messaging, and others (example: Windows Live, Yahoo, Google).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760162">online service provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178911">OSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20960_760163_1178911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A provider of online services like email, messaging, and others (example: Windows Live, Yahoo, Google).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760163">OSP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178911">OSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20961_760164_3104903"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The abstract representation of some work (for example, a movie). A media item is defined by its associated metadata (title, author, etc.).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760164">media item</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3104903">elemento multimedia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20977_760304_1178912"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of maintaining connectivity outside of one's usual service or coverage area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760304">roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178912">mobilidade</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20977_760304_2002552"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of maintaining connectivity outside of one's usual service or coverage area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760304">roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2002552">itinerancia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20978_760305_2016061"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A connection that enables the transmission of data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760305">data connection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2016061">conexión de datos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20983_761626_2016166"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A call that originates from your mobile device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="761626">outgoing call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2016166">chamada saínte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20984_761629_1520489"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collaborative action, such as sharing, calendar sharing, or using a whiteboard.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="761629">activity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520489">actividade</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2099_2397421_3115149"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A subset of the contents of a data warehouse that tends to contain data focused at the department level, or on a specific business area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2397421">DataMart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3115149">data mart</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2099_418571_3115149"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A subset of the contents of a data warehouse that tends to contain data focused at the department level, or on a specific business area.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="418571">data mart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3115149">data mart</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20992_762951_1520582"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email that a customer does not want delivered to their inbox, including spam and phishing messages (identified by the mail service) and messages from blocked senders and domains.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="762951">junk e-mail</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520582">correo lixo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20992_762956_1520582"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email that a customer does not want delivered to their inbox, including spam and phishing messages (identified by the mail service) and messages from blocked senders and domains.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="762956">junk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520582">correo lixo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="20998_763011_1374632"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of colors and background images that lets users change the appearance of Windows Live pages. The theme is common to all pages, except for group, event, and space pages, which may each have their own theme.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763011">theme</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1374632">tema</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21_216347_1674564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that can be used in a workflow rule or template as a placeholder for specific values or text in an email. When you send an email, these placeholders are replaced with the data that meet the conditions that have been set in the workflow rule. For example, if you send an email to an account holder about a contract cancellation date, you can use a dynamic data field to automatically find and insert the correct cancellation date for that contract.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="216347">dynamic data field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1674564">campo de datos dinámico</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21_216348_1674564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that can be used in a workflow rule or template as a placeholder for specific values or text in an email. When you send an email, these placeholders are replaced with the data that meet the conditions that have been set in the workflow rule. For example, if you send an email to an account holder about a contract cancellation date, you can use a dynamic data field to automatically find and insert the correct cancellation date for that contract.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="216348">slug</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1674564">campo de datos dinámico</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21000_763151_1520366"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Parental consent for a child to use a service, view a website, or communicate with a person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763151">permission</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520366">permiso</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21003_763869_1178913"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SmartArt graphic layout type that includes layouts designed to show nonsequential information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763869">List</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178913">Lista</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21004_763870_1178914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SmartArt graphic layout type that includes layouts designed to show steps in a process or timeline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763870">Process</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178914">Proceso</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21005_763871_1178915"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SmartArt graphic layout type that includes layouts designed to show a continual process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763871">Cycle</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178915">Ciclo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21008_763874_1178916"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A SmartArt graphic layout type that includes layouts designed to show how parts relate to a whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763874">Matrix</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178916">Matriz</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21010_763876_3074984"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The overall design of a page or content set, including text elements, controls, and graphics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763876">layout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3074984">deseño</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21012_1135481_1520369"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The descriptive information about a user that is shown to other users. This editable information is separate from the registration information they provide to establish their Windows Live account. This separation allows users to disclose or conceal personal information as they choose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1135481">Windows Live Profile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520369">perfil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21012_763878_1520369"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The descriptive information about a user that is shown to other users. This editable information is separate from the registration information they provide to establish their Windows Live account. This separation allows users to disclose or conceal personal information as they choose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763878">profile</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520369">perfil</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21013_763879_1555496"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An answer that only the user knows for a specific question. The answer is used to confirm someone's identity if they forget their password.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763879">secret answer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1555496">resposta secreta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21015_2392175_3104935"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email address to which password reset information can be sent if a customer forgets the password portion of their Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2392175">alternate email address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3104935">correo electrónico alternativo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21015_3103949_3104935"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An email address to which password reset information can be sent if a customer forgets the password portion of their Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3103949">alternate email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3104935">correo electrónico alternativo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21019_763886_1520386"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A horizontal grouping of actions that apply to the container (or containers) with which the toolbar is associated. For example, a container in which mail is viewed might have an action toolbar with options that include Reply, Delete, and Move to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763886">toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520386">barra de ferramentas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="21022_1216839_1950378"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The user role that is assigned to a user account, which determines the options that are visible to that user and the tasks that the user can perform in the management interface for Exchange Labs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1216839">RBAC role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><te