s available to users. Also, a set of PSTN usage records that define what types of calls are authorized.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1743096">voice policies</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1764175">políticas de voz</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33054_1743100_1787123"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of client version rules that defines the actions to be taken when users try to log on with specific clients and client versions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1743100">client version policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1787123">política de versións do cliente</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33055_1743112_1759712"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A call that bypasses the Mediation Server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1743112">bypass call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1759712">chamada directa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="gra