 app that's downloaded from the Microsoft Store and installed automatically to the PC when a user attaches a certified device to the PC, provided that the device manufacturer has submitted the app to the Microsoft Store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1776723">Microsoft Store device app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1779850">aplicación de dispositivo de Microsoft Store</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33387_1776725_1779814"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of look-and-feel elements (type, color, icons, etc.) that create a sense of brand and a cohesive user experience with Microsoft products.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1776725">Microsoft design language</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1779814">linguaxe de deseño de Microsoft</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="33396_1776952_3026458"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to the Windows Runtime.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1776952">WinRT</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3