ective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178699">libre</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38711_2255081_2255503"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any type of unwanted, unsolicited, telephone call. Common types of nuisance calls include prank calls, telemarketing calls, and silent calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255081">nuisance call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255503">chamada molesta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38712_2255107_2255504"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard layout in which the onscreen keyboard can be split into two halves, resulting into two halves of the keyboard towards the edge of the screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255107">split keyboard mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255504">modo de teclado dividido</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="