 Sway button that resets all the Share options back to their original settings and generates a new URL for the selected sway, revoking access from everyone besides the owner.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396315">Stop sharing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2399000">Parar de compartir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42359_2396316_2398999"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Sway button that allows users to password-protect a particular sway.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396316">Require a password</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2398999">Requirir un contrasinal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4236_16880_1950042"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process an operating system uses to detect and record security-related events, such as an attempt to create, to access, or to delete objects such as files and directories. The records of such events are stored in a file known as a security log, whose contents are available only to those with the proper clearance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16880">auditing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type=