g of edits within documents, shared editable templates, and rich content editing options.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858228">Microsoft Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866071">Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50497_2858228_2866072"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A component-based document model for developers who create collaborative text editing apps that includes options for real-time sharing of edits within documents, shared editable templates, and rich content editing options.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858228">Microsoft Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866072">Microsoft Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50497_2858231_2866071"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A component-based document model for developers who create collaborative text editing apps that includes options for real-time sharing of edits within documents, shared editable templates, and rich content editing options.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858231">Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866071">Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50497_2858231_2866072"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A component-based document model for developers who create collaborative text editing apps that includes options for real-time sharing of edits within documents, shared editable templates, and rich content editing options.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858231">Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866072">Microsoft Fluid Framework</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50498_2858264_2859827"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The number of hours the person spent in meetings with at least one other person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858264">meeting hours</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859827">horas de reunións</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50499_2858268_2859823"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The number of hours the person spent sending and reading email.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858268">email hours</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859823">horas de correo electrónico</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50500_2858270_2859830"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The lack of opposition between work and other life roles. It is the state of equilibrium in which demands of personal life, professional life, and family life are equal.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858270">work-life balance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859830">equilibrio entre o traballo e a vida privada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50501_2858273_2860306"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">When referring to a manager, or to a meeting involving a manager, "skip-level" refers to the employee's manager's manager, sometimes referred to as "second line manager". A skip-level manager is the manager of the employee's manager. A skip-level meeting is a meeting between an employee and the manager of his or her manager.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858273">skip-level</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860306">salto de nivel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50502_2858291_2859822"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collective name for character images with multiple poses, emotions and props.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2858291">cutout people</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859822">persoas recortadas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50505_2859316_2865914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The application that manages Microsoft Volume Licensing Fulfillment and Subscription orders.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859316">MS License</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865914">MS License</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50505_2859320_2865914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The application that manages Microsoft Volume Licensing Fulfillment and Subscription orders.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2859320">Microsoft License</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865914">MS License</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50507_2860396_2861973"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A function in Office apps for mobile phones that allows users to make content (text, buttons, etc.) larger.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860396">large content viewer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861973">visualizador de contido de gran tamaño</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50508_2860488_2861161"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows users to import their financial transactions into Excel so they can view and organize their finances in one place and obtain personalized insights.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860488">Money in Excel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861161">Moeda en Excel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50509_2860564_2861167"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft marketing campaign to promote The Art of Teamwork [50467], a framework, toolkit, and digital curriculum to equip our customers with the tools to practice the five key dynamics to successful teamwork.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860564">The Art of Teamwork Campaign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861167">Campaña A arte do traballo en equipo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50510_2860565_2861165"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Collaboration between members of a group organized around a common responsibility, interest, or objective.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860565">teamwork</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861165">traballo en equipo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50512_2860581_2861169"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability to enter into situations that involve risk and emotional exposure.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860581">vulnerability</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861169">vulnerabilidade</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50513_2860582_2861168"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feeling that ensues from knowing you can be vulnerable with someone without being put down or hurt.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860582">trust</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861168">confianza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50515_2860603_2861964"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Function in Office applications that allows users to select stock images.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860603">content picker</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861964">selector de contido</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50516_2860604_2861970"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of PowerPoint slides, often with supporting notes, that can be shared as a stand-alone document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860604">slide deck</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861970">baralla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50516_2860604_2861976"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of PowerPoint slides, often with supporting notes, that can be shared as a stand-alone document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860604">slide deck</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861976">baralla para arrastrar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50516_2860605_2861970"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of PowerPoint slides, often with supporting notes, that can be shared as a stand-alone document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860605">deck</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861970">baralla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50516_2860605_2861976"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of PowerPoint slides, often with supporting notes, that can be shared as a stand-alone document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860605">deck</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861976">baralla para arrastrar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50517_2860606_2861974"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pane that shows the objects that have been inserted into an Office document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860606">Selection Pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861974">panel de selección</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50518_2860607_2861972"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows the user to edit text by drawing on the screen with a digital pen or with a finger.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860607">intelligent pen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861972">lapis intelixente</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50519_2860771_2861967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of machine learning capabilities that enable users to create models that process structured and unstructured documents to extract information, and classify and automatically tag content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860771">content understanding</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861967">comprensión de contido</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50521_2860780_2861171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Shadow Stack security feature that prevents a class of vulnerabilities known as Return-Oriented Programming (ROP) and requires hardware in order to work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860780">hardware-enforced stack protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861171">protección de pila aplicada mediante hardware</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50521_2860780_3020650"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Shadow Stack security feature that prevents a class of vulnerabilities known as Return-Oriented Programming (ROP) and requires hardware in order to work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2860780">hardware-enforced stack protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3020650">HSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50521_3019770_2861171"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Shadow Stack security feature that prevents a class of vulnerabilities known as Return-Oriented Programming (ROP) and requires hardware in order to work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3019770">HSP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861171">protección de pila aplicada mediante hardware</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50521_3019770_3020650"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows Shadow Stack security feature that prevents a class of vulnerabilities known as Return-Oriented Programming (ROP) and requires hardware in order to work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3019770">HSP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3020650">HSP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50524_2861024_2862260"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Power Mixed Reality feature that allows users to place a 3D object of a specific size into the AR environment around them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861024">AR Cube</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862260">Cubo de RA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50525_2861025_2862262"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Combining nearby pins together to form one new cluster pin, usually with a number of pins provided, to indicate the density of locations for a certain zoom level on the map.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861025">pin clustering</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862262">clústeres de marcador</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50526_2861026_2862261"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pins combined together on the map to form one new cluster pin, instead of showing a bunch of individual pins on top of each other, to indicate the density of locations for a certain zoom level.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861026">cluster pin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862261">marcador de clúster</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50527_2861027_2862263"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The function of tilting the pitch to the map relative to the horizon.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861027">pitch control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862263">control de distancia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50531_2861482_2867123"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To extract data from another service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2861482">scrape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867123">extraer</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50539_2862041_2862254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A web-hosted technology product such as file storage, webmail, search engines, and calendar management.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862041">service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862254">servizo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50540_2862042_2862253"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft web-hosted technology product such as Bing, MSN, OneDrive, Outlook.com, Devices, and Profile, all of which are accessed via a Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862042">Microsoft Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862253">servizo de Microsoft</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50541_2862043_2862255"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A cryptographic algorithm used to create a hash value with 64 hexadecimal characters, or the hash value itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862043">SHA-256</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862255">SHA-256</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50543_2862396_2862904"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The personalized information stream feature of Microsoft Launcher that includes news, events from the user's calendar, photos, notes, contacts, recently-launched apps, and more.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862396">feed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862904">fonte</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50544_2862397_2862906"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Launcher page consisting of a card that has been pinned to the Home screen providing a full-screen experience to card users with all filters and sorting preserved as of the moment the page was pinned.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862397">pinned page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862906">páxina fixada</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50547_2862401_2862905"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Microsoft Edge that notifies users whenever a password that they have saved through the browser has been identified as compromised.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862401">Password Monitor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862905">Monitor de contrasinais</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50548_2862405_2862907"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Edge feature that allows users to select, copy, and paste content that they find across the Web while maintaining the source site's formatting, spacing, and text so the copy looks like the original.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862405">Smart copy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862907">Copia intelixente</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50549_2862409_2862908"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that lets Microsoft Edge users move their horizontal tabs at the top of the browser to a vertical pane at the right side of their screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862409">vertical tabs</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862908">separadores verticais</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50556_2862646_2862915"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Microsoft Stream that allows users with admin rights to mark specific videos to ensure that they appear on the Stream portal when users log in.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862646">spotlight</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862915">sección de contido destacado</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50557_2862647_2862916"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To mark specific videos to ensure that they appear on the Microsoft Stream portal when users log in.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862647">spotlight</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862916">destacar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50558_2862648_2862909"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The page showing new and trending content within a Microsoft Stream group.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862648">Highlights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862909">Contido destacado</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50559_2862649_2862914"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of renewing one's energy over the course of a full night's sleep.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862649">nightly recharge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862914">recarga nocturna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50560_2862871_2863998"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A section of the UI in which the user can store interface elements such as links to apps, folders, or messages in order to keep them in an easily accessible location.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2862871">dock</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2863998">dock</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50568_2863799_2864237"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of topics connected through shared resources and contributors that combines AI with human moderation to help your organization learn about itself.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2863799">knowledge network</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864237">rede de coñecementos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50570_2864253_2867119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A growing catalog of cloud apps that are ranked and scored based on industry standards.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864253">cloud app catalog</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867119">catálogo de aplicacións na nube</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50571_2864257_2867120"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A metric that measures the net adds of customers meeting specified criteria during a reporting period.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864257">customer adds</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867120">incorporacións de clientes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50572_2864258_2864553"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A daily personalized email sent by Cortana to Office 365 users containing tasks and commitments made by the user, a summary of the user's meetings, and relevant documents for the user's day, all using information extracted from the user's Office 365 messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864258">Cortana Briefing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864553">Informe de Cortana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50572_2864258_2864554"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A daily personalized email sent by Cortana to Office 365 users containing tasks and commitments made by the user, a summary of the user's meetings, and relevant documents for the user's day, all using information extracted from the user's Office 365 messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864258">Cortana Briefing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864554">correo electrónico do Informe de Cortana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50572_2864259_2864553"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A daily personalized email sent by Cortana to Office 365 users containing tasks and commitments made by the user, a summary of the user's meetings, and relevant documents for the user's day, all using information extracted from the user's Office 365 messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864259">Cortana Briefing email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864553">Informe de Cortana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50572_2864259_2864554"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A daily personalized email sent by Cortana to Office 365 users containing tasks and commitments made by the user, a summary of the user's meetings, and relevant documents for the user's day, all using information extracted from the user's Office 365 messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864259">Cortana Briefing email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864554">correo electrónico do Informe de Cortana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50578_2864897_2865266"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that protects sensitive information on disk and makes it inaccessible to attackers when the device is locked using encryption keys that are temporarily wiped from the device and only made available when the device is unlocked.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864897">personal information encryption</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865266">cifraxe de información persoal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50578_2864898_2865266"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that protects sensitive information on disk and makes it inaccessible to attackers when the device is locked using encryption keys that are temporarily wiped from the device and only made available when the device is unlocked.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864898">Data Protection under Lock</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865266">cifraxe de información persoal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50578_2864899_2865266"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that protects sensitive information on disk and makes it inaccessible to attackers when the device is locked using encryption keys that are temporarily wiped from the device and only made available when the device is unlocked.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864899">DPL</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865266">cifraxe de información persoal</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50579_2864948_2865261"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The option in Microsoft Photos that allows the user to adjust the brightest part of a photo to be either darker or brighter.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2864948">Highlights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865261">Realces</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50591_2865796_2866067"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A headless app in the Microsoft Store that contains OpenGL and OpenCL API mapping layers on top of DirectX 12 that enable OpenCL and OpenGL apps to run with GPU acceleration in environments where there is no IHV OpenCL or OpenGL driver (for example, on Windows 10 ARM-based PCs).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2865796">OpenCL™ and OpenGL® Compatibility Pack</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866067">Paquete de compatibilidade de OpenCL™ e OpenGL®</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5060_129154_498063"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In relational database management systems, a logical table created through the specification of one or more relational operations on one or more tables. A view is equivalent to a divided relation in the relational model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="129154">view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498063">visualización</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50604_2866253_2866622"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user who has high business impact or access to sensitive information, so they get additional mail flow or security monitoring.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866253">priority user</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866622">usuario prioritario</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50605_2866396_2880850"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of calculation items that are grouped together to reduce the number of redundant measures using the same calculations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866396">calculation group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880850">grupo de cálculo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5061_180517_2470440"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The adherence to stated standards.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="180517">compliance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2470440">cumprimento</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50653_2866963_2880858"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tabular mode system configuration that can improve query performance in high-concurrency scenarios.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866963">query interleaving</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880858">intercalado de consultas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50654_2866964_2880851"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Partner Center model in which partners associate their organization to both a customer and the individual workloads (Microsoft Teams, for example) they are assisting customers to deploy or adopt.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866964">Claiming Partner of Record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880851">asociado solicitante do rexistro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50654_2866964_2880852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Partner Center model in which partners associate their organization to both a customer and the individual workloads (Microsoft Teams, for example) they are assisting customers to deploy or adopt.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866964">Claiming Partner of Record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880852">CPOR</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50654_2866965_2880851"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Partner Center model in which partners associate their organization to both a customer and the individual workloads (Microsoft Teams, for example) they are assisting customers to deploy or adopt.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866965">CPOR</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880851">asociado solicitante do rexistro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50654_2866965_2880852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Partner Center model in which partners associate their organization to both a customer and the individual workloads (Microsoft Teams, for example) they are assisting customers to deploy or adopt.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2866965">CPOR</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880852">CPOR</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50664_2867741_2880856"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that is made available under a license that grants all users access to the source code to the software (rather than just the binary code) and grants some rights to modify the source code and rights to distribute such modifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867741">OSS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880856">software de código aberto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50664_2867741_2880857"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that is made available under a license that grants all users access to the source code to the software (rather than just the binary code) and grants some rights to modify the source code and rights to distribute such modifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867741">OSS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880857">OSS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50664_2867742_2880856"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that is made available under a license that grants all users access to the source code to the software (rather than just the binary code) and grants some rights to modify the source code and rights to distribute such modifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867742">open-source software</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880856">software de código aberto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50664_2867742_2880857"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Software that is made available under a license that grants all users access to the source code to the software (rather than just the binary code) and grants some rights to modify the source code and rights to distribute such modifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867742">open-source software</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880857">OSS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50665_2867743_2880855"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dedicated device in which certain features of the device are restricted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867743">kiosk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880855">pantalla completa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50666_2867744_2867826"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The option in Microsoft Edge in which a customer can copy a URL and paste as a visual link, which provides a card with a key image and title, as well as additional information from the page where available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867744">web preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867826">previsualización web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50667_2867745_2880853"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The capability that provides insights about potential threats using deep collection and analysis to prevent users from being compromised by malicious files and URLs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2867745">detonation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2880853">detonación</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50670_2868303_2869940"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A web script that is placed on an openly accessible web server to allow an adversary to use the web server as a gateway into a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868303">web shell</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2869940">shell web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50671_2868399_2886491"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An employee, usually with no formal training or educational background in computer science, who works on the frontlines of an organization and develop creative solutions to improve business operations with user-friendly technology.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868399">citizen developer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2886491">programador cidadán</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50672_2868545_2870907"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Two apps that are grouped together by the customer, so both apps open at the same time.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868545">app group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870907">grupo de aplicacións</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50673_2868546_2870921"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To enlarge an app on a dual-screen device so that it goes across both screens.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868546">maximize</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870921">maximizar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50674_2868547_2870919"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reorient a dual-screen device that is folded in order to see the other screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868547">flip</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870919">voltear</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50675_2868548_2870920"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To move one screen of a dual-screen device backward.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868548">fold</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870920">dobrar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50679_2868550_2870908"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that has been designed specifically for dual-screen devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868550">Dual-screen enhanced app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870908">aplicación mellorada para dúas pantallas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50681_2868552_2870911"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The hinge that holds the two screens together on the Surface Duo dual-screen device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868552">Dynamic 360° Hinge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2870911">Dynamic 360° Hinge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50682_2868553_2868851"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program designed to reward eligible partners for driving incremental Office 365 and Azure growth along with adherence to tracked management metric KPIs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868553">Accelerated Growth Incentives</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868851">Accelerated Growth Incentives</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50683_2868554_2868894"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft program designed to reward partners for driving consumption of Microsoft Azure services that have been purchased via EA, CASA/EES, MOSA, OSPA, and OSSA.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868554">Azure Incentives</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868894">Azure Incentives</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50684_2868555_2868938"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft initiative designed to give solution providers an opportunity to earn supplemental revenue when they assist end customers with software selection and implementation of Microsoft Dynamics CRM.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868555">Certified Software Advisor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868938">Certified Software Advisor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50684_2898928_2868938"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft initiative designed to give solution providers an opportunity to earn supplemental revenue when they assist end customers with software selection and implementation of Microsoft Dynamics CRM.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2898928">CSA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868938">Certified Software Advisor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50685_2868556_2868982"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program designed to reward Commercial Distributor partners for driving Open License and Office FPP/ESD revenue through resellers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868556">Commercial Distributor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868982">Commercial Distributor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50686_2868557_2869071"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program designed to reward and support CSP direct bill partners for driving the activation and enablement of customers with Microsoft-based Online Services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868557">CSP Direct Bill Partner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2869071">CSP Direct Bill Partner</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50687_2868558_2869159"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program for Cloud Solution Provider (CSP) partners that engage with a two-tier provider, commonly a distributor or hoster, who maintains the relationship with Microsoft and provides additional functions and services that the partner does not.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868558">CSP Indirect Provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2869159">CSP Indirect Provider</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50688_2868559_2869245"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program for Cloud Solution Provider (CSP) resellers that are engaged by indirect CSP partners, who maintain the relationship with Microsoft, and who provide additional functions and services that the indirect CSP partner does not.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868559">CSP Indirect Reseller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2869245">CSP Indirect Reseller</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50689_2868560_2869393"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft incentive program designed to reward LSPs for securing and maintaining annuity relationships with Enterprise customers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2868560">Enterprise Incentives</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2869393">Enterprise Incentives</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_160054_498283"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="160054">color-space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498283">conversión de espazo de cor</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5069_210048_498283"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technique for converting a color in one color space to another color space. Typically, this conversion is from YUV colors from a video source to RGB for display.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210048">color space conversion</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl