 with a command-line interface that is used to control many internal computer functions, such as running programs and organizing and maintaining files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="82028">MS-DOS operating system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497811">MS-DOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5371_82029_497810"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft computer operating system with a command-line interface that is used to control many internal computer functions, such as running programs and organizing and maintaining files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="82029">Microsoft Disk Operating System</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497810">sistema operativo MS-DOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5371_82029_497811"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft computer operating system with a command-line interface that is used to control many internal computer functions, such as running programs and organizing and maintaining files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="82029">Microsoft Disk Operating System</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular<