es, such as from the laptop to a mobile phone and vice-versa, without any interruption in call service or quality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057914">endpoint transfer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058673">transferencia entre extremos</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53721_3057915_3058681"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A conversation method that uses a button to switch a device from the voice transmission mode to the voice reception mode.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057915">push-to-talk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058681">premer para falar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Other</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53721_3057916_3058681"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A conversation method that uses a button to switch a device from the voice transmission mode to the voice reception mode.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3057916">push to talk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3058681">premer para falar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</ter