ows players to work together as teammates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3089283">co-op</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3090056">cooperativo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54165_3090866_3091255"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an attack simulation training, the percentage of users who are compromised by a simulated attack.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3090866">compromise rate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091255">taxa de usuarios afectados</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54166_3090867_3091261"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Part of the Microsoft Project product family, it provides simple, powerful work management capabilities to meet most needs and roles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3090867">Project for the web</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091261">Project para a web</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54167_3090868_3091253"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The built-in Microsoft 365 service that helps administrators secure and manage users' mobile devices such as smartphones and tablets that are used to access work email, calendar, contacts, and documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3090868">Basic Mobility and Security</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091253">Mobilidade e seguranza básicas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54170_3091308_3091643"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of phishing attack that uses telephony to trick users into revealing personal information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091308">vishing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091643">suplantación de identidade telefónica</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54171_3091309_3091641"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an organization, activity, or event that reduces the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere more than it creates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091309">carbon negative</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091641">pegada de carbono negativa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54172_3091310_3091645"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an organization, activity, or event that returns more water to the ecosystem than it removes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091310">water positive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091645">reabastecemento positivo da auga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="54189_3091439_3091507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Fuel obtained from organic raw materials, such as wood, energy plants, algae. It is used for transport, electricity production and heating as a result of the dynamic development of the use of renewable energy sources.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091439">biomass fuel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3091507">combustible de biomasa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGen