P</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5725_295557_498743"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a process that is performed by a person, rather than automated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="295557">manual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498743">manual</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5726_269749_1178199"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A state in which users fill out forms when working offline.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="269749">offline mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1178199">modo sen conexión</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5728_25995_497387"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that enables a broadband connection to the Internet by using cable television infrastructure. Access speeds vary greatly, with a maximum throughput of 10 megabits per second (Mbps).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25995">cable modem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497387">módem por cable</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="573_231958_498439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of coordinates that a cell occupies on a worksheet. For example, the reference of the cell that appears at the intersection of column B and row 3 is B3.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231958">cell reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498439">referencia de cela</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5731_155920_1660336"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of preventing a denial of service attack by limiting the number of requests that can be made to a system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="155920">throttling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1660336">limitación de solicitudes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5731_1645777_1660336"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of preventing a denial of service attack by limiting the number of requests that can be made to a system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1645777">request throttling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1660336">limitación de solicitudes</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5738_44359_497534"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To eliminate text, a file, or part of a document with the intention of removing the information permanently.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44359">delete</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="497534">eliminar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5747_522108_1707025"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server running Lync Server or Office Communications Server that resides in the perimeter network and routes traffic between the internal deployment and users who sign in from outside the firewall.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="522108">edge server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1707025">servidor edge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5754_228518_498431"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The difference between two values, such as the difference between estimated and actual expenses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="228518">variance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498431">diferenza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5759_235060_498528"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Control Panel item that allows the user to view saved networks and reconnect to them.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="235060">Saved networks</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="gl"><ntig><termGrp><term id="498528">Redes gardadas</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">ESP</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5761_7364_1950017"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A phone number that subscribers can dial to reach online services.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7364">access number</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></lang